{"name":"Going Rouge","hex":"#ab858f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"going","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of go","Attending or visiting (a stated event, place, etc.) habitually or regularly."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A departure.","The suitability of ground for riding, walking etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/going"},{"term":"rouge","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a reddish pink colour."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Red or pink makeup to add colour to the cheeks; blusher.","Any reddish pink colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rouge"}],"entries":[{"title":"Going Rouge","blocks":[{"text":"Going Rouge: Sarah Palin, An American Nightmare is a collection of essays about Sarah Palin with a spoof title and book cover design intended to lampoon Palin's memoir Going Rogue: An American Life. It was released on November 17, 2009. Both books feature Palin on the front in red, but Going Rouge has her against a backdrop of black thunder clouds and lightning, instead of the blue sky and white clouds on her memoir."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/48/GoingRogueAnAmericanNightmareSpoofBook.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Going_Rouge","wikidata":"Q5577833"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/42/GoingRogue.jpg/120px-GoingRogue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/42/GoingRogue.jpg/250px-GoingRogue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/42/GoingRogue.jpg/120px-GoingRogue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGoingRogue.jpg